WEBVTT

00:22.001 --> 00:24.371
A TRUE WARRIOR

00:43.391 --> 00:45.601
Don't get cocky.

01:03.041 --> 01:04.581
Who is he?

01:18.971 --> 01:19.801
He's coming.

01:20.851 --> 01:22.261
What are we going to do, Bjorn?

01:53.801 --> 01:57.261
This is bad. Bjorn's gone mad.

02:01.801 --> 02:03.931
Stop him. He'll destroy the ship.

02:04.011 --> 02:06.311
You're crazy.

02:06.391 --> 02:08.941
How are we supposed to stop a monster like that?

02:09.021 --> 02:11.811
Run. No one can stop him now.

02:18.361 --> 02:20.991
He's eaten a berserker mushroom.

02:53.811 --> 02:55.571
All with his bare hands...

02:55.861 --> 02:58.281
He's stronger than a monster.

02:59.031 --> 03:01.991
The Troll of Jom.

03:04.781 --> 03:07.371
All right. One more ship.

03:18.591 --> 03:20.341
They're here.

03:20.421 --> 03:22.641
-What are we going to do?
-Surrender?

03:25.721 --> 03:28.311
Damn it. Come on.

03:28.391 --> 03:30.641
I'd rather die fighting than be a slave.

03:30.731 --> 03:33.901
Listen. Capture the kids alive.

03:33.981 --> 03:37.651
If they get hurt, they won't sell for a high price.
Be careful.

03:47.281 --> 03:49.541
We're going to have some fun with you.

03:57.841 --> 03:59.051
Bjorn?

04:07.391 --> 04:08.311
Thors.

04:17.861 --> 04:21.991
Listen. You've already lost half of your forces.

04:22.651 --> 04:25.661
Leave now, and I won't take your life.

06:04.841 --> 06:06.761
Be gone, pirates.

06:06.841 --> 06:08.841
You cannot defeat me.

06:10.471 --> 06:12.471
-That bastard.
-Stop.

06:12.851 --> 06:15.721
Don't shoot until Askeladd gives the signal.

06:16.021 --> 06:17.771
What are they doing?

06:17.851 --> 06:19.691
We've got the high ground.

06:19.771 --> 06:21.611
What are they stalling for?

06:23.401 --> 06:25.611
What a crazy man.

06:26.111 --> 06:29.611
He's not afraid to take on two whole warships alone.

06:30.071 --> 06:31.701
Let's fight too.

06:31.781 --> 06:34.581
Fool. You amateurs will make things worse.

06:35.331 --> 06:37.911
Their archers are waiting up on the cliff.

06:38.581 --> 06:41.581
He's the one who knows how to handle this.

06:41.671 --> 06:43.591
But...

06:43.841 --> 06:45.211
Don't you understand?

06:45.301 --> 06:46.841
Except for Thors,

06:46.921 --> 06:49.301
we're just a bunch of kids and amateurs.

06:49.971 --> 06:52.181
All we can do is let him handle this.

06:57.271 --> 07:01.561
It looks like they're not
the type of men to leave when I say so.

07:02.101 --> 07:05.071
The archers up on the cliff aren't firing yet.

07:05.731 --> 07:07.781
There's 30 men to the front.

07:07.861 --> 07:10.321
I know I could kill that many myself.

07:11.281 --> 07:13.321
But our ships are close.

07:13.571 --> 07:17.201
If they all jumped over to our ship,
it'd be a free-for-all.

07:18.661 --> 07:20.661
I'd be fine if I was alone, but...

07:32.261 --> 07:33.641
Are you the leader?

07:34.681 --> 07:37.011
In the name of Odin, the Almighty,

07:37.101 --> 07:39.101
I challenge you to a duel.

07:42.771 --> 07:45.191
If you win, you can do whatever you want.

07:45.271 --> 07:48.231
If I win, you must withdraw at once.

07:48.321 --> 07:49.901
If you refuse,

07:49.991 --> 07:52.991
then you're going to lose three times as many men

07:53.071 --> 07:55.701
to capture a mere 12 slaves.

08:00.541 --> 08:02.331
Can I ask you something?

08:03.541 --> 08:05.541
Why do you think I'm their leader?

08:10.671 --> 08:11.631
I can smell it.

08:14.181 --> 08:15.801
Impressive.

08:16.391 --> 08:18.971
All right. I accept the duel.

08:19.431 --> 08:23.311
I, Askeladd, son of Olaf, swear in the name of Odin.

08:23.981 --> 08:26.061
Stay back near the ship's bow.

08:26.151 --> 08:27.561
Okay.

08:45.751 --> 08:46.881
I too

08:47.921 --> 08:50.751
can smell something about you.

08:51.341 --> 08:53.131
You have the same smell as me,

08:53.761 --> 08:55.681
Troll of Jom.

08:57.051 --> 08:58.301
He knows who I am?

09:00.681 --> 09:01.891
Did Floki do this?

09:03.181 --> 09:06.771
You're quick. I like smart men.

09:07.151 --> 09:10.441
My father isn't a bad man like you.

09:10.521 --> 09:11.861
Hey. Stay back.

09:11.941 --> 09:14.951
My father is strong. Die, you pirate.

09:15.031 --> 09:17.111
You idiot. You idiot. Your armor looks weird.

09:18.571 --> 09:21.161
What an energetic boy. Is that your son?

09:22.541 --> 09:24.451
Stop. You fool.

09:24.541 --> 09:27.421
Askeladd. Do you have a wife and children?

09:29.081 --> 09:29.961
No.

09:31.711 --> 09:32.711
I see.

09:34.421 --> 09:35.421
Let's begin.

09:46.061 --> 09:48.981
He's closing up the distance carelessly.

10:18.181 --> 10:19.011
Too shallow.

10:29.351 --> 10:30.851
You're amazing.

10:30.941 --> 10:33.481
No one can beat Askeladd.

10:34.071 --> 10:35.691
Father.

10:39.111 --> 10:42.241
He dodged it. My moment of opportunity...

10:42.871 --> 10:45.331
A surprise attack won't work on him anymore.

10:45.871 --> 10:50.001
Coming all this way was worth it.

10:50.461 --> 10:53.211
He's an incredible man.

10:53.881 --> 10:55.211
Thors...

10:56.671 --> 10:57.881
You're strong.

11:02.971 --> 11:04.641
Forgive me, Askeladd.

11:05.311 --> 11:06.891
I can't go easy on you.

11:08.311 --> 11:10.891
I'm happy to hear that, Thors.

11:24.201 --> 11:25.241
What?

11:25.331 --> 11:26.411
Hey, hey.

11:42.261 --> 11:44.341
Amazing. It's a one-sided fight.

11:46.761 --> 11:49.021
Askeladd is in trouble.

11:49.101 --> 11:52.481
But he's able to block all his attacks.

11:52.851 --> 11:55.981
Father. Kill him.

12:01.281 --> 12:02.281
Oh, no.

12:02.951 --> 12:06.161
He's going after my sword. It won't hold up for long.

12:07.911 --> 12:09.161
That must mean...

12:09.241 --> 12:10.621
His sword is also...

12:12.961 --> 12:14.001
This is it.

12:19.591 --> 12:21.761
Since I know his target,

12:21.841 --> 12:24.471
I can predict the arc of his sword.

12:24.551 --> 12:26.471
This is it. A wide swing.

12:33.811 --> 12:35.441
I fell for his trap.

12:35.521 --> 12:38.401
He was waiting for me to get careless,
and swing wide.

12:38.691 --> 12:41.321
He was planning to have me snap his sword,
all along.

12:41.401 --> 12:43.651
Everything went according to his plan.

12:44.031 --> 12:45.531
Unbelievable.

12:45.611 --> 12:48.451
I can't believe I fell for it.

12:49.121 --> 12:50.541
You did it.

12:50.621 --> 12:54.161
-Thors. You did it.
-That was amazing, Father.

12:54.251 --> 12:55.541
You won.

13:00.211 --> 13:02.421
What's wrong? Kill me.

13:03.471 --> 13:05.381
I don't need to.

13:05.471 --> 13:07.551
Say you surrender. That's enough for me.

13:09.681 --> 13:11.561
I'm their leader.

13:12.181 --> 13:14.561
I can't say that in front of my men.

13:22.821 --> 13:24.821
What's wrong? Kill me.

13:24.901 --> 13:26.661
If you don't kill me,

13:26.741 --> 13:28.871
this duel will never end.

13:39.041 --> 13:42.001
Ouch, my head hurts.

13:45.801 --> 13:48.971
What? What's going on?

13:54.391 --> 13:55.521
Askeladd...

13:56.561 --> 13:57.601
Defeat?

13:58.311 --> 13:59.901
He lost?

14:00.561 --> 14:03.861
Admit it. I won this duel.

14:03.941 --> 14:05.531
Withdraw your troops at once.

14:07.651 --> 14:09.781
You really are strong, Thors.

14:10.241 --> 14:12.911
You could lead a whole army.

14:15.251 --> 14:17.041
But why?

14:17.121 --> 14:21.171
Why did you stay in Iceland for 15 years,
even though you're such a strong warrior?

14:21.841 --> 14:23.801
Don't you think you're wasting your skills?

14:24.131 --> 14:25.301
No.

14:28.801 --> 14:31.261
I must rely on a sword like this,

14:32.351 --> 14:34.311
because I am not yet a master.

14:35.971 --> 14:37.771
A true warrior

14:38.231 --> 14:39.481
doesn't need a sword.

14:51.741 --> 14:53.201
Thors, you...

14:54.701 --> 14:56.701
Why don't you become our leader?

15:16.561 --> 15:19.231
Just kidding. Hey, hey.

15:19.311 --> 15:21.731
Why isn't anyone laughing? I was just joking.

15:24.311 --> 15:26.361
What? He was joking?

15:28.191 --> 15:30.991
This is no time for...

15:31.071 --> 15:33.991
joking around with a straight face.

15:38.581 --> 15:40.371
Don't move.

15:40.461 --> 15:42.791
I'll cut the kid's head off.

15:42.871 --> 15:44.131
Let go of your sword.

15:44.211 --> 15:45.921
Hurry up.

15:47.421 --> 15:49.261
Askeladd. You bastard.

15:50.471 --> 15:52.511
Father.

15:58.601 --> 16:00.891
Come on. You're such a good man.

16:01.561 --> 16:04.401
Did you think we were going
to follow the rules of the duel?

16:07.651 --> 16:10.321
I was just playing around with you.

16:10.401 --> 16:13.951
I wanted to find out
how good the famous Troll of Jom really was.

16:14.031 --> 16:15.701
I had a good time.

16:39.261 --> 16:40.221
Askeladd.

16:41.221 --> 16:43.851
You broke the rules of the duel.

16:44.561 --> 16:46.731
I won this match.

16:48.521 --> 16:50.071
Who cares?

16:50.151 --> 16:52.571
I'm after your head.

16:53.701 --> 16:54.701
I know.

17:14.971 --> 17:16.221
I accept.

17:18.851 --> 17:20.391
The winner of this duel...

17:22.271 --> 17:23.891
is you.

17:35.281 --> 17:39.571
Father!

17:53.211 --> 17:54.421
Father...

17:56.931 --> 17:58.591
Askeladd.

17:58.681 --> 18:00.971
I won this duel.

18:02.181 --> 18:04.601
Keep the promise you made as a warrior.

18:06.681 --> 18:07.941
I know.

18:08.021 --> 18:10.811
In the name of my ancestor Artorius,

18:10.901 --> 18:12.691
I shall withdraw my troops at once.

18:17.611 --> 18:20.951
Leif. I have a favor to ask you.

18:23.581 --> 18:26.661
Bring my head to Sigvaldi,

18:26.751 --> 18:28.961
the leader of the Jomsvikings.

18:29.501 --> 18:33.461
If he suspects that I disappeared
to avoid his summons,

18:33.801 --> 18:35.841
he'll take his revenge by punishing the village.

18:36.801 --> 18:38.721
You're a crazy man.

18:44.811 --> 18:46.391
You bastard.

18:46.931 --> 18:49.851
I'll give you my life. Just like you wanted.

18:50.901 --> 18:52.861
Let that child go right now.

18:56.691 --> 18:59.281
Father. Father.

19:18.631 --> 19:19.671
I'm glad.

19:21.091 --> 19:22.341
For now...

19:39.821 --> 19:41.491
Damn kid.

19:42.241 --> 19:44.621
You should start valuing your life.

19:45.491 --> 19:47.871
You should be grateful to Thors.

19:47.951 --> 19:51.921
He was a man who was worth more
than a hundred bratty kids like you.

20:06.261 --> 20:08.471
Father died.

20:10.521 --> 20:12.941
Father was so strong.

20:14.851 --> 20:16.691
Why did he let go of his sword?

20:17.731 --> 20:20.571
How could he say a warrior doesn't need a sword?

20:21.611 --> 20:23.571
That can't be true.

20:25.911 --> 20:27.741
Why...?

20:27.831 --> 20:29.541
Why did Father...?

20:30.831 --> 20:32.621
Damn.

20:32.711 --> 20:34.461
He...

20:34.541 --> 20:36.831
He lost to Father.

20:36.921 --> 20:38.801
Damn it.

20:38.881 --> 20:40.961
Why was my father the one who died?

20:41.051 --> 20:43.341
Why is he the one who's still alive?

20:44.181 --> 20:45.341
Damn it.

20:46.391 --> 20:48.181
Damn it all.

20:56.441 --> 20:58.821
I'm surprised they abandoned these nice ships.

20:58.901 --> 21:00.981
It must have been a big decision.

21:01.071 --> 21:04.361
They can't move the ship without Thors.

21:04.451 --> 21:07.161
Thors could row as hard as five men.

21:07.241 --> 21:08.571
Really?

21:11.741 --> 21:13.711
Things worked out well.

21:13.791 --> 21:15.541
I was wanting to get a third ship.

21:22.461 --> 21:24.631
Twenty-eight men injured.

21:24.721 --> 21:25.551
How many died?

21:26.631 --> 21:29.891
None? Not even one? Impossible.

21:32.521 --> 21:33.851
Askeladd.

21:34.481 --> 21:35.441
Hey.

21:35.941 --> 21:39.151
Come to the stern. Askeladd.

21:39.611 --> 21:42.731
What do you want? Shut up already.

21:51.911 --> 21:53.411
It's Thors' kid.

21:53.791 --> 21:55.791
He was hiding inside the ship.

21:55.871 --> 22:00.081
Look at him. The kid's got a dagger.

22:00.171 --> 22:04.711
He's going to kill us.

22:07.631 --> 22:10.551
Oh, no. I'm so scared.

22:11.971 --> 22:13.311
How dare you...?

22:14.721 --> 22:15.851
How dare you...?

22:15.931 --> 22:19.311
How dare you kill Father?

22:20.191 --> 22:22.151
I'm going to kill you.

22:22.231 --> 22:24.481
I'm going to kill you, no matter what.

22:24.571 --> 22:27.201
I'm going to kill you!

22:29.161 --> 22:32.831
I'm going to kill you!

22:35.831 --> 22:36.951
He's just a kid.

22:37.041 --> 22:39.581
But that look in his eyes...

22:42.541 --> 22:44.801
What do you want to do, Askeladd?

22:44.881 --> 22:46.591
Shall we throw him overboard?

22:48.591 --> 22:49.971
Leave him.

22:51.391 --> 22:53.011
He will die soon anyway.

23:00.811 --> 23:02.111
Father...
